                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "43015786-1d39-4415-85b5-7dc6784c977a",
                        "entry_id": "63d9d697-d8a1-3ca8-9ebb-2933871ccfc2",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Draconic"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19596f4c-47f9-306c-8c07-640ae44aede6",
                        "entry_id": "63d9d697-d8a1-3ca8-9ebb-2933871ccfc2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of draconic (“very severe or strict; draconian”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9eacb5c3-1731-4661-9aa5-eebaf64ee313",
                                "sense_id": "19596f4c-47f9-306c-8c07-640ae44aede6",
                                "text": "[…] they no land / Doom'd to bewail the blasphemy of laws / Making kings' rights divine, by some Draconic clause."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06bfa2e3-d73f-44d3-b0a9-e2e5c662daa8",
                                "sense_id": "19596f4c-47f9-306c-8c07-640ae44aede6",
                                "text": "Beggars, cut-purses, swindlers, tavern-bilks, broken life-guardsmen, foreign counts, native highwaymen, and some poor honest unfortunates, the victims of a Draconic law of debtor and creditor, all found their Patmos turn out to be a mere shifting quicksand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "996c7f6f-5998-4437-b2da-75a08f918315",
                                "sense_id": "19596f4c-47f9-306c-8c07-640ae44aede6",
                                "text": "The inference is, therefore, that they were all the property of this Nicholas de la Reynie, who was, as I understand, the gentleman specially concerned with the maintenance and execution of the Draconic laws of that epoch."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
